<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX5-QA4-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX5-QA4-001" ;
  triage:title "record_task_outcome duplicates the outcome stats match block and cooldown stamp verbatim in its write-failure and write-success paths" ;
  triage:description "AX.5 QA-4 (quality-mgr ax5-qa-r4, PR #1201 Final Quality Report 2026-09-05T15:36Z) at head 4e9f6602fd8c37340cced7e4c7725aae48434ea9; rust-qa-agent observation, recorded by fenix per the no-dismissal rule at minor severity. After the AX5-QA3-005 fix, record_task_outcome (crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs:555-578) contains two byte-for-byte identical match outcome blocks followed by self.stamp_task_attempt(member, now), one inside the if !record_task_reminder(..) early-return branch and one after it. Behaviour is correct and covered by ax5_10, but the duplication is exactly the drift surface that produced AX5-QA3-005. Fix: collapse to a single shared block (compute the write result, then run one match+stamp), keeping the 32 herdr_queue_wake tests green. Consolidated-cleanup default applies: fix on the highest open sprint branch (AX.6) or in the CLEANUP pass, not by reopening AX.5." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "RUST-QA" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
